{"name":"Chlorosis","hex":"#75876e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"chlorosis","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An anaemia, due to deficiency of iron, characterized by a yellow-green coloration of the skin.","A yellowing of plant tissue due to loss or absence of chlorophyll."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chlorosis"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chlorosis","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, chlorosis is a condition in which leaves produce insufficient chlorophyll. As chlorophyll is responsible for the green color of leaves, chlorotic leaves are pale, yellow, or yellow-white. The affected plant has little or no ability to manufacture carbohydrates through photosynthesis and may die unless the cause of its chlorophyll insufficiency is treated and this may lead to a plant disease called rusts, although some chlorotic plants, such as the albino Arabidopsis thaliana mutant ppi2, are viable if supplied with exogenous sucrose."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/AlbinoPopcorn.jpg/330px-AlbinoPopcorn.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chlorosis"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Sweetgum-leaf-interveinal-chlorosis.jpg/500px-Sweetgum-leaf-interveinal-chlorosis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Sweetgum-leaf-interveinal-chlorosis.jpg/500px-Sweetgum-leaf-interveinal-chlorosis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Liquidambar leaf with interveinal chlorosis","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASweetgum-leaf-interveinal-chlorosis.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Citrus_limon_chlorosis.jpg/500px-Citrus_limon_chlorosis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thu